From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Raevsky <valentin@compulab.co.il>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: maxim-serdes: add opt-in multi-link default routes

The ADI deserializer framework initializes only the first enabled GMSL
input route. Tegra capture channels select their upstream stream by the
deserializer's CSI-2 frame descriptor during notifier completion. A
four-camera overlay therefore leaves channels for virtual channels 1-3
without a corresponding active route, before an application can configure
the experimental userspace Streams API.

Add the local compulab,default-multi-link-routes boolean property to opt
into one initial active route for every enabled GMSL input. Aggregate all
inputs on the first enabled CSI output PHY and allocate a distinct source
stream on that shared source pad. Keep each input on its native stream 0;
the existing ADI hardware routing and virtual-channel remapping determine
the corresponding CSI-2 output virtual channels.

Use the existing route array sized for MAX_DES_NUM_LINKS. Leave the
first-input-only default unchanged for profiles without the property.
This establishes initial routes; it does not enable capture or alter the
serializer/sensor power and streaming callbacks.

Document the opt-in property and numbered endpoints on a shared CSI-2
output PHY. Their endpoint IDs distinguish the Tegra virtual-channel
connections; all endpoints still map to the same hardware source pad and
must describe the same physical lane configuration and link frequency.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CompuLab Tegra default stream aggregation]
Signed-off-by: Valentin Raevsky <valentin@compulab.co.il>
---
 .../bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96712.yaml      | 22 ++++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96712.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96712.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96712.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96712.yaml
@@ -42,6 +42,13 @@ properties:
   enable-gpios: true
 
+  compulab,default-multi-link-routes:
+    description: |
+      Initialize a route for each enabled GMSL input to the first enabled
+      CSI-2 output PHY, using a separate source stream for each input.
+      Without this local option, initialize only the first enabled input.
+    type: boolean
+
   maxim,control-channel-port:
     description:
       Selects which deserializer control-channel port is connected to the
       upstream I2C segment when the device resets. 0 selects port 0, 1 selects
@@ -85,10 +92,21 @@ properties:
       '^port@[4-7]$':
         $ref: /schemas/graph.yaml#/$defs/port-base
         unevaluatedProperties: false
-        description: CSI-2 Output port 0-3
+        description: |
+          CSI-2 output PHY. Each numbered endpoint represents a logical
+          virtual-channel connection to a separate receiver channel on
+          the same source pad. All endpoints describe the same physical
+          bus, including its lane layout and link frequency.
 
         properties:
-          endpoint:
+          '#address-cells':
+            const: 1
+
+          '#size-cells':
+            const: 0
+
+        patternProperties:
+          '^endpoint(@[0-3])?$':
             $ref: /schemas/media/video-interfaces.yaml#
             unevaluatedProperties: false
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c b/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <linux/i2c-atr.h>
 #include <linux/i2c-mux.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/sched.h>
 #include <linux/units.h>
@@ -2579,6 +2580,8 @@ static int max_des_init_state(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	struct max_des *des = priv->des;
 	struct max_des_phy *phy = NULL;
+	bool default_multi_link_routes = device_property_read_bool(priv->dev,
+					"compulab,default-multi-link-routes");
 	unsigned int stream = 0;
 	unsigned int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < des->info->num_phys; i++) {
@@ -2606,12 +2609,12 @@ static int max_des_init_state(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 		stream++;
 
 		/*
-		 * The Streams API is an experimental feature.
-		 * If multiple routes are provided here, userspace will not be
-		 * able to configure them unless the Streams API is enabled.
-		 * Provide a single route until it is enabled.
+		 * Keep the experimental Streams API opt-in for ordinary profiles.
+		 * EDGEDES aggregation needs one stream per enabled GMSL link
+		 * before Tegra initializes the capture channels.
 		 */
-		break;
+		if (!default_multi_link_routes)
+			break;
 	}
 
 	return __max_des_set_routing(sd, state, &routing);
-- 
2.34.1
